# Geometry Nodes — Coding Conventions

Review all geometry-node diffs against these rules and `.clang-tidy`.

## SPDX headers

Every new or modified `.cc`/`.hh` file must start with:

```
/* SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2023 Blender Authors
 *
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later */
```

## File and namespace naming

- New nodes: `source/blender/nodes/geometry/nodes/node_geo_<snake_case>.cc`
- Namespace must match the file: `node_geo_foo.cc` → `namespace blender::nodes::node_geo_foo_cc`
- Prefer the fully-qualified form over nested `namespace blender { namespace nodes::... }`
- Primary include: `"node_geometry_util.hh"`

## Build registration

- Add the `.cc` to `source/blender/nodes/geometry/CMakeLists.txt` `SRC` list (alphabetically)
- End the file with `static void node_register() { ... }` and `NOD_REGISTER_NODE(node_register)`
- Do not manually edit `node_register.cc` or `register_geometry_nodes.cc` (auto-generated)

## Node identity and type IDs

- RNA idname: `"GeometryNode<PascalCase>"_ustr`
- New nodes: omit legacy type in `geo_node_type_base()` — do not add `GEO_NODE_*` to `BKE_node_legacy_types.hh` unless required for versioning or `switch (node->type_legacy)` cases
- If a node is added, verify CMakeLists and any required type-ID / enum entries are updated together

## String conventions (`_ustr` vs `const char*`)

- Geometry node API (`node_declare`, `GeoNodeExecParams`): use `"Socket Name"_ustr` literals
- Compositor `NodeOperation` (`get_input`, `get_result`): plain `const char*` string literals
- User-visible strings: `N_()`, `TIP_()`, `IFACE_()` — never hardcode English without a translation macro

## Performance and style

- Flag heap allocations (`new`, `MEM_new`, `std::make_unique`, container growth) inside per-element loops (e.g. over points, faces, curves)
- Prefer `const T &` over `T &` when the parameter is not modified
- Follow `.clang-tidy` readability and bugprone checks where applicable

## Review output

- Comment inline on the specific offending line
- If the diff is clean, post one line: "Geometry node conventions: no issues found."
